The reference and workbench execute exactly the same number of shifts, adds and multiplies on the regex fixture. The trace shows a better target. Three bounds checks compare the same `state` against 9 in the copy-and-clear loop. Each executes 64 times, and none has a credited reduction. I’ll test whether the existing range analysis can prove the later checks redundant.
